==Spanish==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|es|la|videō|vidēre}}, from {{inh|es|itc-pro|*widēō||to see}}, ultimately from {{der|es|ine-pro|*weyd-}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|view}}, {{m|en|wit}}, {{m|en|wise}}. Compare the borrowed doublet {{doublet|es|vídeo|notext=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr|+<audio:LL-Q1321 (spa)-Rodelar-ver.wav>}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb}}

# {{lb|es|transitive|literally}} to [[see]], to [[spot]]
#: {{ux|es|Vine, '''vi''', vencí.|I came, I '''saw''', I conquered.}}
#: {{ux|es|Sí, con mis propios ojos, lo '''vi''' robar el dinero.|Yes, with my own eyes, I '''saw''' him steal the money.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[see]], to [[look at]], to [[view]] {{gl|perceive}}
#: {{ux|es|Hmm. Ya '''veo'''...|Hmm. I '''see'''...}}
#: {{ux|es|Tal experiencia única en la vida cambiará tu manera de '''ver''' el mundo.|Such a once in a lifetime experience will change the way that you '''look at''' [or '''see''' or '''view'''] the world.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[see]], to [[tell]], to [[observe]]
#: {{ux|es|Puedo '''ver''' que no eres como el resto.|I can '''tell''' you aren't like the rest of them.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[see]], to [[check]] {{gl|verify}}
#: {{ux|es|Déjenme '''ver''' si hay moros en la costa.|Let me '''check''' if the coast is clear.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[watch]]
#: {{ux|es|'''ver''' la televisión|'''to watch''' television}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive}} to [[look]], to [[seem]]
#: {{ux|es|'''Te ves''' tan diferente desde la última vez que te vi.|You '''look''' so different since the last time I saw you.}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive}} to [[see]] oneself, to [[picture]] oneself
#: {{ux|es|'''Me veo''' así como un consejero, nada más.|I just '''see myself''' as an advisor, nothing more.}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive}} to [[find]] oneself, to [[be]]
#: {{ux|es|'''Nos vemos''' obligados a hacernos una pregunta difícil.|We '''are''' forced to ask ourselves a difficult question.}}
# {{lb|es|reciprocal}} to [[see]] one another
#: {{ux|es|'''Nos vemos'''!|See you!|lit=We'll '''see each other'''!)}}

====Conjugation====
This is one of three verbs to have an irregular indicative imperfect, alongside {{m|es|ser}} and {{m|es|ir}}. ''Ver'''s imperfect is a remnant of the Old Spanish {{m|es|veer}} (only the stem ''ve-'' is irregular, otherwise the endings are still regular). In some old texts and in rural speech the archaic preterite forms ''vide'' and ''vido'' can be found instead of the current ''vi'' and ''vio'' forms.
